  <iati-identifier>GB-COH-2153193-GB-COH-2153193-ALERT-KIBERA</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-COH-2153193" secondary-reporter="0" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Alert</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Urban Flood Resilience - Integrating Community Perspectives in Kibera</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2015 and 2016 KDI is working together with residents to build the resilience of communities in Kibera to adapt and respond to flooding. The overall objective of this project is to create a &#xE2;&#x20AC;&#x153;toolkit&#xE2;&#x20AC;&#x9D; that can be used to implement flood risk reduction strategies in Kibera (and ultimately in other informal settlements) while incorporating local perspectives. The toolkit will comprise reliable data and information from the community level, flood mapping developed through hydrological modelling and physical surveying, flood risk assessment incorporating community perspectives on risk, and policy prescriptions for applying the tools in Kibera and elsewhere.International Alert are committed to providing a third party review on the project in 2016. In addition International Alert have been providing pro-bono support to the development of the consultation methodology and household survey with regard to vulnerability, environmental risk and conflict issues. This has been a contribution from their Environment, Climate Change and Security program.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The poorest and most vulnerable residents in Kibera, affected by heavy flooding causing death and destruction annually.</narrative>
  </description>
